From e9067e8aef2c0416f05fc5a3d66ea13d05104f32 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Taimoor Ul Islam <tislam@iastate.edu>
Date: Mon, 29 Jun 2026 12:03:05 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 11/54] kaiair: IPC-DL Tier-A, decoupled per-PDSCH power
 actuator + HARQ-ACK closed loop

Adds the gNB-only (Tier-A) downlink power-control path for PktR, in two
increments, both validated on hardware (USRP X310, single UE).

Increment 1, decoupled per-PDSCH actuator (env-gated):
- Override pdsch.tx_pwr_info.pwr_ctrl_offset on the two C-RNTI data builders
  INDEPENDENTLY of the CSI-RS RRC value, so the UE's CQI assumption is
  unchanged (no confound). KAIAIR_PKTR_DL_ACTUATE / KAIAIR_PKTR_DL_PWR_OFFSET.
- HW: moving the offset moves real delivered DL power (MCS24+15 collapsed the
  link with the UE still told powerControlOffset=0). Boosting clips (the lower
  PHY keeps ~12 dB PAPR headroom), so authority is shed-only, actuator output
  is clamped to [0,15] (never negative -> never clips).

Increment 2, closed loop (pktr_dl_power_controller):
- Per-UE Robbins-Monro / OLLA-style controller driven by per-packet HARQ-ACK,
  holding empirical DL BLER at the PktR target (1 - beta): ack -> shed,
  nack -> add power; converges to BLER = 1 - beta. Fed from ue_cell
  handle_dl_ack_info, applied per grant in ue_cell_grid_allocator.
  KAIAIR_PKTR_DL_LOOP / KAIAIR_PKTR_DL_ETA / KAIAIR_PKTR_DL_NOMINAL_DB.
- HW (beta=0.9): loop shed offset 0->15 and regulated DL delivery to ~90% (=beta)
  vs ~96% over-provisioned with the loop off, same throughput, ~15 dB less power.

Unit tests: pktr_dl_power_controller_test (7), pktr_runtime_config_test (+5 DL).
